3. HOW DO YOU GET PROMOTED TO A MANAGEMENT POSITION IN THE CIVIL SERVICE?
Requirements:
•    to be appointed to a Class I civil service position;
•    at least 5 years of professional experience in the field of study required for the civil service position, for appointment to the management positions of head of service and secretary general of a commune, as well as to equivalent specific civil service positions;
•    at least 7 years of professional experience in the field of study required for the civil service position, for appointment to management positions other than those referred to above;

3. HOW DO YOU GET PROMOTED TO A MANAGEMENT POSITION IN THE CIVIL SERVICE?
Requirements:
•    to be appointed to a Class I civil service position;
•    at least 5 years of professional experience in the field of study required for the civil service position, for appointment to the management positions of head of service and secretary general of a commune, as well as to equivalent specific civil service positions;
•    at least 7 years of professional experience in the field of study required for the civil service position, for appointment to management positions other than those referred to above;
•    to meet the education and professional experience requirements prescribed by law for occupying the civil service position;

